\subsection{An Approximately Linear Relation Between $\sqrt{D_{\rm KL}}$ and Reward}
\label{sec:KL}
In Figures \ref{fig:RobustnessRL} and \ref{fig:KLvsReward} we observe an \emph{approximately linear relation} between $\sqrt{\mathrm{KL}}$ and PM score during RLHF training.  Furthermore, we note that when all models are trained and evaluated with the same PMs, the learning curves are roughly \emph{parallel} in the $\sqrt{D_{\rm KL}}$-reward plane. Note that here the `KL' is more precisely $D_{\rm KL}(\pi || \pi_0)$, where $\pi$ denotes the policy distribution (and $\pi_0$ the initial policy), as evaluated empirically on the samples drawn from the policy during training.

