If we have access to a small number of examples of Harmlessness inputs (the out-distribution), we could perform a few-shot outlier exposure, as first proposed by \cite{https://doi.org/10.48550/arxiv.1812.04606}. \cite{thulasidasan2021a} suggests using a single class representing the OOD examples. \cite{fort2021exploring} has used outlier exposure on top of individually strong near-OOD detectors and showed that they still enjoy a large benefit from being exposed to the examples of the out-distribution. We observe a similar benefit here, as discussed in detail in Section~\ref{app:OOD} and shown in Figure~\ref{fig:OOD_outlier_exposure}.  
